        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "How many real solutions does the equation \\(\\arcsin x=2\\arctan x\\) have?",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "Since \\(\\arcsin x\\) is defined for \\(x\\in[-1,1]\\), put \\(x=\\sin\\theta\\), where \\(\\theta\\in[-\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{\\pi}{2}]\\). The equation becomes \\(\\arctan(\\sin\\theta)=\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\). Taking tangent gives \\(\\sin\\theta=\\tan\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\). With \\(t=\\tan\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\), this becomes \\(t=\\frac{2t}{1+t^2}\\), so \\(t(t^2-1)=0\\). Thus \\(\\theta=-\\frac{\\pi}{2},0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\), yielding \\(x=-1,0,1\\).",
        "question_audio": null,
